# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What must never be committed.
#
# The rule that bit this repo: an anchored pattern only matches at the root. `/out/` let
# `fpga/out/` (148 MB, written by a script that ran with fpga/ as its cwd) escape entirely.
# Every rule below that names a build product is therefore UNANCHORED, so it matches at any
# depth, and the few that really are root-only are marked as such.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- run artifacts -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Labs write run directories, consoles, traces and captures here. Large, regenerable, and
# never evidence on their own -- the evidence is the committed results row plus the archive.
out/
runs/

# --- the evidence archive ------------------------------------------------------------------
# A symlink to a directory outside the repo, so `git clean` and a lab that wipes its own run
# directory cannot reach it.
/archive

# --- Vivado ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project trees, checkpoints, journals and logs: hundreds of files and hundreds of MB per
# build, all reproducible from tcl/ + the vendored Verilog. The .bit files ARE tracked (see
# fpga/pynq-z2/bitstreams.csv) so the hardware labs run without a Vivado licence.
.Xil/
proj/
*.dcp
*.jou
*.str
*.rpt
*.pb
*.wdb
*.vcd.gz
vivado*.log
vivado_pid*.str
hs_err_pid*.log
.Xil*/
NA/
fpga/pynq-z2/build_*/proj/
fpga/pynq-z2/build_*/reports/
# ps7_init.{h,html,tcl} are Vivado exports regenerated with every block design write; only
# ps7_init.c is tracked, because the host loader reads it.
ps7_init.h
ps7_init.html
ps7_init.tcl

# --- Verilator / C++ sim ----------------------------------------------------------------
# obj_dir is Verilator's default; this repo also uses obj_<name> per testbench. Both carry
# generated C++, objects, archives and linked executables -- these HAVE been committed here
# by accident before.
obj_dir/
obj_*/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.d

# --- Zephyr / CMake / west ----------------------------------------------------------------
build/
build-*/
twister-out*/
.west/
zephyr-chipyard-sw/tools/
zephyr-chipyard-sw/tools-manual/
zephyr-chipyard-sw/zephyr_ws/modules/
zephyr-chipyard-sw/zephyr_ws/tools/
zephyr-chipyard-sw/zephyr_ws/bootloader/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
compile_commands.json

# --- third-party build trees --------------------------------------------------------------
/third_party/riscv-isa-sim/build/
/third_party/tacit-decoder/target/

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- which board THIS checkout drives -----------------------------------------------------
# Per-machine and deliberately untracked: env.sh reads it when PYNQ_HOST is unset.
# board.conf.example IS tracked and is the documentation.
/board.conf

# --- secrets --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Bedrock key (scripts/93_bedrock_key.sh) and the seat list. Unanchored on purpose: a key
# written from any cwd must not be committable.
secrets/
bedrock.env
bedrock.env.previous
aws/bedrock/seats.txt

# --- locks ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.locks/
.board*.lock
.board*.lock.queue/

# --- editor / OS noise ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
